<code>assert !this.empty() => (\result == null && this.elementAt(this.size() - 1) == null) || \result.equals(this.elementAt(this.size() - 1));</code>--------------------<code>assert !this.empty() => (this.peek() == null && this.elementAt(size() - 1) == null) || this.peek().equals(this.elementAt(size() - 1));</code>--------------------<code>assert !this.empty() => this.peek() == this.elementAt(this.size() - 1);</code>

This assert statement captures the condition that if the stack is not empty, the result of `peek()` should be equal to the last element of the stack, which is accessed using `elementAt(this.size() - 1)`.--------------------